2. Coaxial Cable
What is Coaxial Cable?

Coaxial cable is a copper cable designed to carry high-frequency signals.

It has multiple layers.

Structure:

Outer Protective Layer

        |
        |
Metal Shield

        |
        |
Insulator

        |
        |
Copper Core
Why is it called Coaxial?

Because all layers share the same axis.

"Co" = same

"Axial" = axis

Uses of Coaxial Cable

Used in:

Cable TV
Internet connections
CCTV systems
Radio transmission
Advantages
Better shielding than twisted pair
Less interference
Longer distance
Disadvantages
