3. Fiber Optic Cable

Now the most important modern transmission medium.

What is Fiber Optic Cable?

Fiber optic cable transfers data using light signals instead of electrical signals.

It uses extremely thin strands of glass or plastic.

Structure
Outer Jacket

      |
      |
Cladding

      |
      |
Glass Core

      |
