Types of Fiber Optic Cable
1. Single Mode Fiber (SMF)

Characteristics:

Very thin core
One light path
Very long distance

Used for:

Internet backbone
Undersea cables
Telecom networks

Distance:

Hundreds of kilometers.

2. Multi Mode Fiber (MMF)

Characteristics:

Larger core
Multiple light paths

Used for:

Data centers
Campus networks

Shorter distance than single mode.

Advantages of Fiber Optic
1. Extremely High Speed

Supports:

Gigabit speeds
Terabit speeds
2. Long Distance

Can transmit data over huge distances.

3. No Electromagnetic Interference

Because it uses light, electrical noise does not affect it.

4. More Secure

It is harder to intercept compared to copper cables.

Disadvantages
Expensive installation
Difficult to repair
Requires specialized equipment
